Subject: [PATCH 10678/11362] Third data-borne-marker quarantine today: it is a
 whole lineage, not three accidents

exp6856 (sealed risk-sensitive learning audit) is the third artifact today stamped
flagged_adversarial for DURATION_TOO_SHORT while declaring a deterministic CPU
substrate. Verified the same way as the other two: four compute markers, all as data
keys, none in any declaration field. Here the context is a
leave_one_family_out_portability check whose observed map is keyed by model family.

Times: exp6840 09:23Z, exp6853 18:29Z, exp6856 20:22Z.

The framing changes with the third. All three belong to the residual-memory and
risk-sensitive-learning lineage, whose analysis is per model family -- leave-one-out
portability, per-family means, family-keyed split manifests. An experiment whose
independent variable IS the model family necessarily carries model names as data
keys, so every artifact it produces trips a whole-blob marker scan. The mis-flagging
is structural to the lineage rather than incidental to three runs.

Recorded a falsifiable prediction so this can be checked instead of assumed: the next
artifact in this lineage that reports per-family results on CPU will also be flagged,
with no change in its honesty. If a later one is not flagged, either the scan was
fixed or that artifact stopped reporting per-family keys, and both are worth knowing.

The cost is compounded by the capstone gap filed at 13:40Z: all three must be skipped
by headline aggregation under the fabrication gate, yet exp6840 was aggregated anyway
by a capstone that lacks the skip check. So the quarantine is both wrongly applied and
unevenly enforced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw

